                                            <div class="mb-5">
                            <h3 class="mb-4">Frequently Asked</h3>
                            <div class="accordion custom-accordion" id="faqAccordion">
                                                                    <div class="accordion-item">
                                        <h3 class="accordion-header" id="headingOne0">
                                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed text_md_18" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseOne0" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapseOne">
                                                <span class="pe-2">What makes a website user-friendly?</span>
                                            </button>
                                        </h3>
                                        <div id="collapseOne0" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingOne">
                                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                                <p class="m-0 text_md_18">A user-friendly website is easy to browse, quick to load, and mobile-friendly. It becomes more convenient for your visitors to find information. Know that - clear structure, minimal clutter, and a smooth browsing experience - are key components.</p>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                                                    <div class="accordion-item">
                                        <h3 class="accordion-header" id="headingOne1">
                                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed text_md_18" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseOne1" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapseOne">
                                                <span class="pe-2">How can I improve the user experience on my website?</span>
                                            </button>
                                        </h3>
                                        <div id="collapseOne1" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingOne">
                                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                                <p class="m-0 text_md_18">A websites User Experience (UX) is built around – <br />
a.	loading speed<br />
b.	mobile responsiveness, <br />
c.	simplified navigation, and enhancing <br />
d.	content readability. <br />
<br />
Regularly conducting user testing and implementing feedback is a must. Future Digit specializes in these strategies. They will offer you solutions based on this, exactly cut to your requirements.</p>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                                                    <div class="accordion-item">
                                        <h3 class="accordion-header" id="headingOne2">
                                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed text_md_18" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseOne2" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapseOne">
                                                <span class="pe-2">Why is a simple website design important for UX?</span>
                                            </button>
                                        </h3>
                                        <div id="collapseOne2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingOne">
                                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                                <p class="m-0 text_md_18">A simple website design allows distraction-free navigation. It allows users to focus on key content or actions. Simple designs improve usability by guiding users with a clear visual hierarchy and intuitive navigation.</p>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                                                    <div class="accordion-item">
                                        <h3 class="accordion-header" id="headingOne3">
                                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed text_md_18" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseOne3" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapseOne">
                                                <span class="pe-2">What is mobile optimization and why does it matter?</span>
                                            </button>
                                        </h3>
                                        <div id="collapseOne3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingOne">
                                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                                <p class="m-0 text_md_18">Mobile optimization means that users will be able to experience the website on their phone. For the ultimate user experience, the website needs to load fast and content must be easy-to-read. Google’s mobile-first indexing gives priority to mobile-friendly websites in search rankings. This makes it important for SEO and user satisfaction.</p>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                                                    <div class="accordion-item">
                                        <h3 class="accordion-header" id="headingOne4">
                                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed text_md_18" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseOne4" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapseOne">
                                                <span class="pe-2">How can a fast-loading website improve user experience?</span>
                                            </button>
                                        </h3>
                                        <div id="collapseOne4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingOne">
                                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                                <p class="m-0 text_md_18">Websites that load quickly prevent user frustration and reduce bounce rates. This can directly impact the SEO and conversion rates. Optimizing images, minimizing redirects, and allowing browser caching are some ways to boost speed.</p>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                                                    <div class="accordion-item">
                                        <h3 class="accordion-header" id="headingOne5">
                                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed text_md_18" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseOne5" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapseOne">
                                                <span class="pe-2">What are the most common website design mistakes to avoid?</span>
                                            </button>
                                        </h3>
                                        <div id="collapseOne5" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingOne">
                                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                                <p class="m-0 text_md_18">Common mistakes include - <br />
<br />
a.	Cluttered layouts<br />
b.	Slow page loading<br />
c.	Poor mobile optimization<br />
d.	Hard-to-find navigation<br />
<br />
A simple website design and consistent branding can avoid these pitfalls.</p>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                                                    <div class="accordion-item">
                                        <h3 class="accordion-header" id="headingOne6">
                                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed text_md_18" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseOne6" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapseOne">
                                                <span class="pe-2">How do I make my website accessible to all users?</span>
                                            </button>
                                        </h3>
                                        <div id="collapseOne6" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingOne">
                                            <div class="accordion-body">
                                                <p class="m-0 text_md_18">To make a website accessible, it should comply with WCAG (Web Content Accessibility Guidelines). This includes –<br />
<br />
a.	Using alt text for images<br />
b.	Allowing keyboard navigation<br />
c.	Providing text alternatives for multimedia content<br />
<br />
Future Digit focuses on creating inclusive websites, ensuring that accessibility is part of the core design process.</p>
                                            </div>
                                        </div>
                                    </div>
                                                            </div>
                        </div>
                    


                    
