<script src="https://www.google.com/recaptcha/api.js"></script>
                <script type="application/ld+json">
        {
          "@context": "https://schema.org",
          "@type": "FAQPage",
          "mainEntity": [{
                        "@type": "Question",
                        "name": "What makes a website user-friendly?",
                        "acceptedAnswer": {
                        "@type": "Answer",
                        "text": "<p>A user-friendly website is easy to browse, quick to load, and mobile-friendly. It becomes more convenient for your visitors to find information. Know that - clear structure, minimal clutter, and a smooth browsing experience - are key components.</p>"
                        }
                    } ,  {
                        "@type": "Question",
                        "name": "How can I improve the user experience on my website?",
                        "acceptedAnswer": {
                        "@type": "Answer",
                        "text": "<p>A websites User Experience (UX) is built around – 
a.	loading speed
b.	mobile responsiveness, 
c.	simplified navigation, and enhancing 
d.	content readability. 

Regularly conducting user testing and implementing feedback is a must. Future Digit specializes in these strategies. They will offer you solutions based on this, exactly cut to your requirements.</p>"
                        }
                    } ,  {
                        "@type": "Question",
                        "name": "Why is a simple website design important for UX?",
                        "acceptedAnswer": {
                        "@type": "Answer",
                        "text": "<p>A simple website design allows distraction-free navigation. It allows users to focus on key content or actions. Simple designs improve usability by guiding users with a clear visual hierarchy and intuitive navigation.</p>"
                        }
                    } ,  {
                        "@type": "Question",
                        "name": "What is mobile optimization and why does it matter?",
                        "acceptedAnswer": {
                        "@type": "Answer",
                        "text": "<p>Mobile optimization means that users will be able to experience the website on their phone. For the ultimate user experience, the website needs to load fast and content must be easy-to-read. Google’s mobile-first indexing gives priority to mobile-friendly websites in search rankings. This makes it important for SEO and user satisfaction.</p>"
                        }
                    } ,  {
                        "@type": "Question",
                        "name": "How can a fast-loading website improve user experience?",
                        "acceptedAnswer": {
                        "@type": "Answer",
                        "text": "<p>Websites that load quickly prevent user frustration and reduce bounce rates. This can directly impact the SEO and conversion rates. Optimizing images, minimizing redirects, and allowing browser caching are some ways to boost speed.</p>"
                        }
                    } ,  {
                        "@type": "Question",
                        "name": "What are the most common website design mistakes to avoid?",
                        "acceptedAnswer": {
                        "@type": "Answer",
                        "text": "<p>Common mistakes include - 

a.	Cluttered layouts
b.	Slow page loading
c.	Poor mobile optimization
d.	Hard-to-find navigation

A simple website design and consistent branding can avoid these pitfalls.</p>"
                        }
                    } ,  {
                        "@type": "Question",
                        "name": "How do I make my website accessible to all users?",
                        "acceptedAnswer": {
                        "@type": "Answer",
                        "text": "<p>To make a website accessible, it should comply with WCAG (Web Content Accessibility Guidelines). This includes –

a.	Using alt text for images
b.	Allowing keyboard navigation
c.	Providing text alternatives for multimedia content

Future Digit focuses on creating inclusive websites, ensuring that accessibility is part of the core design process.</p>"
                        }
                    }  ]}
        </script>
